-- title:
--   Supersingular chart with q+1 ends and linked inertia
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\neq q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asserts that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ (Laurent series over $L$) which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the rational $q$-expansion function field of the group [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the level subgroup being $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\big)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, whose residue field $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A` is algebraically closed, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ carries an $A$-algebra structure compatible with that of $L$. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ be a tame element: `hϖt` gives a unit $u$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=qu$. Let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $\mathsf q^{-1}+\dots$ of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`). Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and `jChartFin A (↥K) j` for $j$ regarded in $C$. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and assume `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   **Terminology used in the conclusion.** For $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, a *level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$* means an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29): for every weight $k\in\mathbb{Z}$, every pair $f,g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms for [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) viewed in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$, every pair of integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ of $f,g$ with the Laurent series of $p_g$ nonzero, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi)=e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\,$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\,$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, where `conjElemN m γ` is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}a&b/m\\ mc&d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}$. Further, [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is the quotient of $\kappa[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`; [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) is the kernel of the character $(g,c)\mapsto \overline{\det g}\cdot c^{q+1}$ on $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{Z}/q)\times\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$, and [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) is its action by $\kappa$-algebra automorphisms on `CoordRing q κ`; [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.redQ q`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L230) is reduction $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})\to\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and `diagOneElem q d` is $\mathrm{diag}(1,d)$. Finally, $\hat A=$ `AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal A) A`, and for $\pi\in\hat A$ the *crossing model* `UVCrossingModel Â π` is $\hat A[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\pi)$, with distinguished elements `UVCrossingModel.U`, `UVCrossingModel.V` and constants `UVCrossingModel.const`.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist an $A$-subalgebra $B\subseteq K$, a valuation subring $W\subseteq K$ and a proof `hBW` that $B\subseteq W$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) $C\le B$.
--
--   (2) Every $f\in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$; thus $K$ is the fraction field of $B$.
--
--   (3) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$.
--
--   (4) $W\cap L=A$: for $x\in L$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $W$ if and only if $x$ is in the image of $A$.
--
--   (5) $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   (6) $W$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (7) For $b\in C$: $b\in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; so $W$ is centred on $y$.
--
--   (8) For $f\in K$: $f\in W$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; so $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the prime $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   (9) (Drinfeld chart.) For every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ there is a ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) which is surjective, has $\rho(b)=0$ exactly for $b\in\mathfrak m_W$, satisfies $\rho(a)=\overline a$ for $a\in A$ (the image of the residue of $a$), and is equivariant in the following sense: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ (i.e. $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$) there are $c\in\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma,c)\in$ `hSubgroup q` such that $\rho(\tau b)=$ `hAction q κ` $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma,c)\,(\rho b)$ for all $b\in B$ with $\tau b\in B$; such that if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity then $c\neq1$; and (linked scalars) such that the same scalar $c$ is realised with trivial matrix part inside $\Gamma(q)$: there are $\gamma'\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau'$ at $\gamma'^{-1}$ preserving $W$, with $(1,c)\in$ `hSubgroup q`, such that $\rho(\tau' b)=$ `hAction q κ`$(1,c)(\rho b)$ for all $b\in B$ with $\tau' b\in B$.
--
--   (10) $B$ is stable under every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   (11) For every prime ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ such that for every $b\in B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ one has $\tau b\in B$ and $\tau b\in Q$.
--
--   (12) If $b\in B$ is such that for all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\tau b\in B$ one has $\tau b\in\mathfrak m_W$, then $\varpi\mid b$ in $B$.
--
--   (13) For $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau$ preserves $y$ on $C$ (for $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$, $b\in y\iff\tau b\in y$), then $\tau$ preserves $W$.
--
--   (14) (Ends.) There exist $n\ge1$ with $n\mid q+1$; $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W$; $m\ge1$ with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t w$ for some unit $w\in A$; $\zeta_0\in\hat A$ with $\zeta_0^n=1$ and $\zeta_0^k-1$ a unit for $0<k<n$; a proof `hjK` that the series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) — the result of substituting $\mathsf q\mapsto\mathsf q^{\,q\ell}$ in the $j$-series — lies in $K$, a proof `hjC` that this element lies in $C$, and $a_0\in A$ with that element minus $a_0$ in $y$; and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$, such that:
--
--   (14a) $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise;
--   (14b) for $0<k<n$ there is $f\in B$ with $\tau_0^k f\neq f$;
--   (14c) every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ agrees on $B$ with $\tau_0^k$ for some $k<n$;
--   (14d) `ends` has exactly $q+1$ elements;
--   (14e) every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$ permutes the ends: for $O\in$ `ends` there is $O'\in$ `ends` with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$;
--   (14f) the action is transitive: for all $O,O'\in$ `ends` there are $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ with $f\in O\iff\tau f\in O'$;
--   (14g) $\tau_0$ preserves each end: $f\in O\iff\tau_0 f\in O$ for $O\in$ `ends`;
--   (14h) distinct ends are distinguished by units: for $O\neq O'$ in `ends` there is $f$ lying in both which is a non-unit of $O$ and a unit of $O'$;
--   (14i) (common chart) there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_c\subseteq K$ of finite type over $A$, stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, such that for every $O\in$ `ends` one has $B_c\subseteq O$ and $O$ is the localisation of $B_c$ at its elements that are units of $O$ (for $f\in K$: $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$);
--   (14j) for $O\in$ `ends`, $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$: if $\tau(O)\subseteq W$ then $\tau$ preserves $W$;
--   (14k) for every $O\in$ `ends`: $O\subseteq W$; $O$ is a Noetherian local ring; $C\subseteq O$; $O\cap L=A$ in the sense of (4); every $f\in O$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_O$ to the image of some $a\in A$ lying in $O$ (that is, $f-a$ is a non-unit of $O$); and, with $\varpi\in O$, there are $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model $\hat A[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1-\varpi^m)$ (which is local), units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of it, and $\zeta_0'$ inverse to $\zeta_0$, such that
--    • $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $O$;
--    • $\iota$ carries the image of each $a\in A$ lying in $O$ to `const` of the image of $a$ in $\hat A$;
--    • $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$;
--    • $c_y$ lies in $\mathfrak m_W$ and $c_x$ does not;
--    • the element `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` $-\,a_0$ lies in $O$ and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the model with $\iota$ of that element equal to $w_V V^{\,e}$;
--    • $\tau_0$ acts through $\theta_0$: for $f\in O$ with $\tau_0 f\in O$, $\iota(\tau_0f)=\theta_0(\iota f)$;
--    • $\theta_0(U)-\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0)U$ and $\theta_0(V)-\mathrm{const}(\zeta_0')V$ both lie in the square of the maximal ideal of the model;
--    • (Igusa branch) there is a valuation subring $W_x\subseteq K$ with $O\subseteq W_x$, $C\subseteq W_x$, $W_x\cap L=A$, $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\varpi$, admitting $t\in W_x$ whose reduction is transcendental in the sense that for every $p\in A[X]$ with $p(t)\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak m_A$; with the same property for the element `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`; with $c_x\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y\notin\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; such that every $b\in C$ lying in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ lies in $y$, while some $b\in y$ is not in $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; such that each other end $O'\neq O$ contains an element outside $W_x$; and such that if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, $\tau$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$, $O'\in$ `ends` and $\tau(O')\subseteq W_x$, then $O'=O$;
--    • (poles) there is an $A$-subalgebra $B_x\subseteq K$ with $B_x\subseteq B\cap O$, of finite type over $A$, stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, such that every $f\in B_x$ satisfies $\mathrm{ord}_P f\ge0$ at every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ with $\mathrm{ord}_P j\ge0$; such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at its elements that are units of $O$; and containing an element $b$ which lies outside every valuation subring $V\subseteq K$ with $V\cap L=A$, with $\varpi\in\mathfrak m_V$, with $j\in V$ such that $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p\in A[X]$ with $p(j)\in V$, and such that some $f\in O$ is not in $V$;
--   (14l) for every valuation subring $V\subseteq K$ with $V\cap L=A$, $C\subseteq V$ and $y\subseteq\mathfrak m_V$: either $B\subseteq V$, or there is $O\in$ `ends` with $O\subseteq V$ and every non-unit of $O$ in $\mathfrak m_V$.
--
--   (15) (Orbit poles.) There is $b\in B$ lying outside every valuation subring $V\subseteq K$ with $V\cap L=A$, with $\varpi\in\mathfrak m_V$, and with $j\in V$ such that $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p\in A[X]$ with $p(j)\in V$.
--
--   (16) (Deck separation.) For every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\varpi$ which is not matched with $y$ by any level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (that is, for no such $\gamma,\tau$ does $b\in y\iff\tau b\in y''$ hold for all $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$), there is $b\in B$ such that for all such $\gamma$ and $\tau$ and every valuation subring $V\subseteq K$ containing $C$ and satisfying: every $c\in C$ with $\tau^{-1}c\in C$ and $\tau^{-1}c\in y''$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$ — one has $b\notin V$.
--
--   (17) (Drinfeld chart with tame inertia.) The clause (9) holds again, and with the following additional property of $\rho$: for every $\pi\in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, every pair of ring automorphisms $\sigma_L$ of $L$ and $\sigma_A$ of $A$ compatible with the structure map $A\to L$ and with $\sigma_A(a)\equiv a \pmod{\mathfrak m_A}$ for all $a$, every $\tilde\alpha\in A$ with $\sigma_A(\pi)=\tilde\alpha\pi$, every $\alpha\in\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ whose image in $\kappa$ is the residue of $\tilde\alpha$, and every ring automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ acting on Laurent coefficients through $\sigma_L$ (the series of $\tau x$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffMap σL`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L16) of the series of $x$, for all $x\in K$): $B$ is $\tau$-stable, $\tau$ preserves $W$, and for every $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ equals $\alpha^{q+1}$, if $(\mathrm{diag}(1,(d^q)^{-1}),\alpha^q)$ lies in `hSubgroup q` then $\rho(\tau b)=$ `hAction q κ` of that element applied to $\rho(b)$, for all $b\in B$ with $\tau b\in B$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, at a supersingular point of the special fibre, of an integral model over a henselian discrete valuation ring of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ with level group the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$: it produces a formally smooth chart $B$ whose special fibre carries a Drinfeld-curve structure compatible with the level automorphisms, together with the $q+1$ ends (crossing-model completions) through that point, their tame inertia and their separation on distinct Igusa branches. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField) in the construction of the semistable model underlying the level-lowering argument.
